---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "November 15, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Azkar Tracker Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Azkar Tracker iOS app. Azkar Tracker collects no data — it stays on your devices and in your own iCloud account."
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="container legal__container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</span>
      <h1>Azkar Tracker Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        Azkar Tracker is built by Zesencia Technologies. This policy is simple because the
        app is simple: <strong>we do not collect, receive, or share any of your data. It
        stays on your devices and, if you use iCloud, in your own private iCloud
        account.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>What We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing. Azkar Tracker has no accounts, no analytics, no tracking, no advertising,
        and no third-party SDKs. The app works fully offline, and the only place your data
        is ever sent is your own private iCloud account, as described below.
      </p>

      <h2>Data Stored on Your Device</h2>
      <p>
        Your zikrs, counts, streaks, goals, and reminders are stored on your device. This
        data is also included in your personal device backups (such as iCloud or computer
        backups), which are under your control.
      </p>

      <h2>iCloud Sync</h2>
      <p>
        If you are signed in to iCloud, Azkar Tracker keeps your zikrs, counts, streaks,
        goals, and reminders in sync across your devices and restores them if you reinstall
        the app. This data is stored in your own private iCloud database using Apple's
        CloudKit service. It is tied to your Apple Account, it is covered by
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>, and we
        have no access to it. App settings such as appearance and accent color are not
        synced.
      </p>
      <p>
        To turn sync off, open the Settings app, tap your name, then iCloud, and switch off
        Azkar Tracker under apps using iCloud. The app keeps working on your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Location</h2>
      <p>
        If you enable prayer-time reminders, the app may ask for permission to use your
        location. Your location is used only on your device to calculate prayer times with a
        built-in solar calculator — it is never transmitted anywhere, and no internet
        connection is used or required. This permission is optional; the app works fully
        without it.
      </p>

      <h2>Notifications</h2>
      <p>
        Reminders are scheduled locally on your device using the system notification
        service. No notification data leaves your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Deleting Your Data</h2>
      <p>
        Deleting the app deletes all of its data from that device. If you use iCloud sync, a
        copy remains in your private iCloud account so it can be restored later. To delete
        it, open the Settings app, tap your name, then iCloud, then Manage Storage (or
        Manage Account Storage), choose Azkar Tracker, and delete its data. Apart from your
        devices and your own iCloud account, there is nothing stored anywhere else.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Because the app collects no data from anyone, it collects no data from children.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        If a future version of the app ever changes how data is handled, we will update this
        page and the "Last updated" date above before that version is released.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at
        {" "}<a href="mailto:hello@zesencia.com">hello@zesencia.com</a>.
      </p>
      <p>Zesencia Technologies is operated by Sublime Trade LLC.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: 96px 120px;
  }

  .legal__container {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal h1 {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }

  .legal__updated {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
